---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CollectionWalkthrough from '../components/marketing-preview/CollectionWalkthrough.astro';
import OperationsStory from '../components/marketing-preview/OperationsStory.astro';
import PilotOffer from '../components/marketing-preview/PilotOffer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="The product | PumpOS fuel station management" description="Explore customer credit, Shift reconciliation, stock records and daily reports. See how PumpOS connects the work at your fuel station." path="/product">
 <section class="page-heading page-heading--split site-container"><div><p class="section-context">Inside PumpOS</p><h1>From the forecourt<br />to the financial record.</h1></div><p>Your station runs on readings, handovers, collections and decisions. Keep the record of that work together.</p></section>
 <nav class="product-links site-container" aria-label="Product sections"><a href="#walkthrough">Credit & collections ↓</a><a href="#shifts">Shifts ↓</a><a href="#stock">Stock ↓</a><a href="#reports">Reports ↓</a><a href="#owner">Owner access ↓</a></nav>
 <div class="content-wrap"><CollectionWalkthrough /></div>
 <div id="shifts"><OperationsStory detailed /></div>
 <section id="stock" class="product-detail site-container"><div><p class="section-context">Stock accountability</p><h2>Know what should be there.<br />Record what actually is.</h2><p>Keep purchase and stock records alongside physical checks. A difference stays visible, with a reason to follow up.</p><ul><li>Fuel Sales derived from Nozzle Readings</li><li>Purchases and stock movements</li><li>Tank Dips, Stock Counts and recorded variance</li></ul><a class="inline-link" href="/demo">See inventory in a demo ↗</a></div><div class="stock-example product-replica" data-product-reveal><div class="replica-title"><span>Tank stock check</span><span>Sample data</span></div><div><h3>Diesel · Tank 1</h3><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stock position</th><th scope="col">Litres</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Expected stock</td><td>12,450.00 L</td></tr><tr><td>Actual stock</td><td>12,420.00 L</td></tr><tr><td>Variance</td><td class="variance-cell">−30.00 L</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Sample check. Investigate and record the reason for the difference.</p></div></div></section>
 <section id="reports" class="product-detail site-container"><div><p class="section-context">Reports with a history</p><h2>The day's report.<br />Kept as it was generated.</h2><p>A Shift Summary records a closed Shift. The Daily Station Sales Report brings together closed-shift summaries and the Business Day's financial records.</p><p style="margin-top:18px">Later financial entries do not silently rewrite the saved DSSR. You can distinguish what was known at generation from what was recorded later.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/docs/running-shifts">Read about Shift close ↗</a></div><div class="report-example product-replica" data-product-reveal><div class="report-example-top"><strong>PumpOS</strong><span>Sample station</span></div><h3>Daily Station<br />Sales Report</h3><p>Business date · 14 Sep 2026</p><dl><div><dt>Shift summaries</dt><dd>2 closed Shifts</dd></div><div><dt>Sales & stock</dt><dd>Recorded for the day</dd></div><div><dt>Financials</dt><dd>As of generation</dd></div><div><dt>Report state</dt><dd>Saved snapshot</dd></div></dl><p>Illustrative report layout · Sample data</p></div></section>
 <section class="access-explainer site-container"><div id="desktop"><p class="section-context">For the station team</p><h2>A focused desktop workspace.</h2><p>Use the desktop app for daily operations, or the web console from a supported browser. Your team records activity and reconciles the Shift in the same system.</p><a href="/download" class="inline-link">Get PumpOS ↗</a></div><div id="owner"><p class="section-context">For the owner</p><h2>Open the record yourself.</h2><p>Review customer balances, financial accounts and reports in the console. The online mobile owner view provides recent financial entries when you're away from your desk. Availability depends on recorded activity and connectivity.</p><a href="/demo" class="inline-link">See the owner view ↗</a></div></section>
 <PilotOffer compact />
</BaseLayout>
